# CTRL-A and CTRL-X on a Visual selection, and g CTRL-A / g CTRL-X (change.txt).

=== v_CTRL-A adds to the first number on each selected line
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_CTRL-A*
quote:  Add [count] to the number or alphabetic character in the highlighted text.
given:
  |1. a 1
  1. b 1
  1. c 1
keys:   Vj<C-a>
expect:
  |2. a 1
  2. b 1
  1. c 1
mode:   normal

=== v_CTRL-A with a count
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_CTRL-A*
quote:  Add [count] to the number or alphabetic character in the highlighted text.
given:
  |1
  1
keys:   Vj5<C-a>
expect:
  |6
  6
mode:   normal

=== v_CTRL-A only sees the selected digits
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_CTRL-A*
quote:  Add [count] to the number or alphabetic character in the highlighted text.
given:  1|234
keys:   vl<C-a>
expect: 1|244
mode:   normal

=== v_CTRL-A puts the cursor at the start of the selection
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_CTRL-A*
quote:  Add [count] to the number or alphabetic character in the highlighted text.
given:
  x 1
  x |1
keys:   Vk<C-a>
expect:
  |x 2
  x 2
mode:   normal

=== v_CTRL-A on just the digits ignores the sign
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_g_CTRL-X*
quote:  To ignore the sign Visually select the number before using CTRL-A or CTRL-X.
given:  x-|5
keys:   v<C-a>
expect: x-|6
mode:   normal

=== v_CTRL-A over the sign counts it
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_g_CTRL-X*
quote:  For decimals a leading negative sign is considered for incrementing or decrementing
given:  x|-5
keys:   vl<C-a>
expect: x|-4
mode:   normal

=== v_CTRL-X subtracts on each line
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_CTRL-X*
quote:  Subtract [count] from the number or alphabetic character in the highlighted text.
given:
  |10
  20
  30
keys:   VG3<C-x>
expect:
  |7
  17
  27
mode:   normal

=== v_CTRL-A skips lines with no number
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_CTRL-A*
quote:  Add [count] to the number or alphabetic character in the highlighted text.
given:
  |1
  none
  1
keys:   VG<C-a>
expect:
  |2
  none
  2
mode:   normal

=== v_CTRL-A in a block selection uses the number in the block
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_CTRL-A*
quote:  Add [count] to the number or alphabetic character in the highlighted text.
given:
  1 |1 1
  1 1 1
keys:   <C-v>j<C-a>
expect:
  1 |2 1
  1 2 1
mode:   normal

=== v_g_CTRL-A makes an incrementing sequence
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_g_CTRL-A*
quote:  Move to the second "1." and Visually select three lines, pressing g CTRL-A results in:
given:
  1.
  |1.
  1.
  1.
keys:   VGg<C-a>
expect:
  1.
  |2.
  3.
  4.
mode:   normal

=== v_g_CTRL-A with a count steps by the count
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_g_CTRL-A*
quote:  each one will be incremented by an additional [count] (so effectively creating a [count] incrementing sequence).
given:
  |0
  0
  0
keys:   VG2g<C-a>
expect:
  |2
  4
  6
mode:   normal

=== v_g_CTRL-A skips a line with no number in the sequence
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_g_CTRL-A*
quote:  If several lines are highlighted, each one will be incremented by an additional [count]
given:
  |0
  x
  0
keys:   VGg<C-a>
expect:
  |1
  x
  2
mode:   normal

=== v_g_CTRL-X makes a decrementing sequence
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_g_CTRL-X*
quote:  each value will be decremented by an additional [count] (so effectively creating a [count] decrementing sequence).
given:
  |10
  10
  10
keys:   VGg<C-x>
expect:
  |9
  8
  7
mode:   normal

=== v_g_CTRL-A on a block column
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_g_CTRL-A*
quote:  Add [count] to the number or alphabetic character in the highlighted text.
given:
  a |0 0
  a 0 0
  a 0 0
keys:   <C-v>jjg<C-a>
expect:
  a |1 0
  a 2 0
  a 3 0
mode:   normal

=== v_g_CTRL-A on hex numbers
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_g_CTRL-A*
quote:  Add [count] to the number or alphabetic character in the highlighted text.
given:
  |0x0e
  0x0e
keys:   Vjg<C-a>
expect:
  |0x0f
  0x10
mode:   normal

=== . repeats v_CTRL-A on the same number of lines
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  Note that when repeating a command that used a Visual selection, the same SIZE of area is used
given:
  |1
  1
  1
keys:   Vj<C-a>
expect:
  |2
  2
  1
dot:
  |3
  3
  1
mode:   normal

=== . repeats v_g_CTRL-A as a sequence
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  Note that when repeating a command that used a Visual selection, the same SIZE of area is used
given:
  |0
  0
keys:   Vjg<C-a>
expect:
  |1
  2
dot:
  |2
  4
mode:   normal

=== u undoes v_CTRL-A on every line
ref:    nvim/change.txt *v_CTRL-A*
quote:  Add [count] to the number or alphabetic character in the highlighted text.
given:
  |1
  1
keys:   Vj<C-a>
expect:
  |2
  2
undo:
  |1
  1
mode:   normal
